From 1fe05a796556db4f7bcdf148a4cf44d12554bb23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christoph Pillmayer
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:36:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pan/bi: Run CSE before load_store_vectorize

opt_load_store_vectorize uses src0 in @load_ubo as entry_key::resource.
Entries targeting different resources end up in different lists of
vectorization candidates and are never vectorized as a result. Running CSE
before exposes loads that target the same resource.

The resource is different because lower_explicit_io loads matrix and
vector components individually with each load having it's own address
computation. For example loading a mat4 for some lighting computation
can turn into 16 @load_ubo instructions. With this patch, they get
turned back into 4 32x4 loads.

The vectorized loads can increase spilling in the following situation:
Before:
   load(a)
   use(a)
   load(b)
   use(b)
After:
   load(a, b)
   use(a)
   use(b)

-> b needs to be live across use(a)
The spill/fill increase is outweighed by the overall LS savings.

Reviewed-by: Lorenzo Rossi
Reviewed-by: Lars-Ivar Hesselberg Simonsen
Reviewed-by: Faith Ekstrand
Reviewed-by: Erik Faye-Lund
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46347>
---
 src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_nir.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_nir.c b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_nir.c
index f43606abab15..0d1c401e7c60 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_nir.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_nir.c
@@ -918,6 +918,12 @@ bifrost_postprocess_nir(nir_shader *nir,
    if (bi_use_kraid(nir, gpu_arch) && nir->info.stage == MESA_SHADER_FRAGMENT)
       NIR_PASS(_, nir, pan_nir_opt_var_tex, gpu_arch);
 
+   /* CSE helps expose loads from the same resource. load_store_vectorize
+    * does not vectorize loads if they are not from the same resource
+    * (determined by the SSA value of the source).
+    */
+   NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_opt_cse);
+
    /* Why aren't we vectorizing nir_var_shader_temp?
     * Basically, the current RA doesn't know rematerialization and is still
     * learning spills, if we vectorize temp stores it might create long-lived
